<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">bash</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">bash</ansi> command performs a shield bash attack during combat, using your shield
as a weapon to damage and potentially knock your opponent to the ground.

<ansi fg="yellow">Requirements:</ansi>

  - Must be in active combat
  - Must have a shield equipped
  - Cannot be used if special move cooldown is active

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">bash</ansi>
  Bash your current combat target with your shield

<ansi fg="yellow">Mechanics:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="stat">Damage:</ansi> 50% of your normal attack damage
  <ansi fg="stat">Knockdown Chance:</ansi> 40% base, modified by opposed skill check
    - Attacker: Weapon Combat skill + Strength
    - Defender: Combat skill + Dexterity
  <ansi fg="stat">Cooldown:</ansi> 5 rounds (shared with trip and kick)
  <ansi fg="stat">Skill:</ansi> Progresses Weapon Combat

If the knockdown succeeds, your target becomes <ansi fg="red">prone</ansi> for a minimum of 1 full
round, suffering attack and defense penalties. See <ansi fg="command">help prone</ansi> for details.

<ansi fg="yellow">See Also:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">help trip</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help kick</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help stand</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help prone</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help combat</ansi>
